[Music]  we begin with that breaking news israel  is accusing hezbollah of launching what  it's calling an  infiltration attempt on its border with  lebanon  it happened in the past couple of hours  in the sheba farms region  there's been no confirmation as yet from  hezbollah that it was behind the  incident the united nations is urging  restraint  from both sides israel's prime minister  benjamin netanyahu was posted on twitter  saying what was happening on the  northern border was being constantly  monitored  he says israel won't allow iran to  establish itself  on the border netanyahu adds that  lebanon and hezbollah will be  responsible  for any attack out of lebanon  we have two correspondents working on  this story harry fawcett is live for us  in west jerusalem in just a few moments  but first let's join zeta hodder who's  on the lebanon side  of that border with israel zainab what's  the latest  a much awaited statement from the  lebanese armed group hezbollah released  just a short while ago hezbollah denying  that there was  any sort of attack in the statement it  says  there was no operation today there was  no  exchange of fire we did not open fire it  was the israelis who opened fire  and the statements adds that the israeli  army is in a state of confusion  we do know that there has been tension  along this border for  the past few days now ever since  it was confirmed that a hezbollah  fighter was killed in what was believed  to be an israeli airstrike in syria  and everyone was waiting for the  possible hezbollah retaliation because  hezbollah promised in the past that any  if any of its fighters are killed in  syria it will  retaliate so hezbollah now saying that  there was no operation  the israeli army initially said that  there was a security incident  and then it went on to explain that  a group of hezbollah fighters tried to  infiltrate the shabbat farm so  conflicting  narratives here on what exactly happened  behind me  behind those hills is shiva farms  a disputed area disputed territory a  land that  intersects syria israel and  lebanon and it's quite significant that  if indeed there was some sort of  operation that hezbollah has now  denied to choose this area because it's  disputed it means that hezbollah does  not want to escalate the situation  any sort of operation there it can  easily justify by saying that it is  defending  lebanese territory in the eyes of  lebanon this territory shabbat farms  belongs to  it uh but the status of shiva has not  been settled by the international  community because lebanon and syria have  still not demarcated  uh their border so hezbollah now saying  that there was no operation and now  saying that it was the israeli army  that's confused  really criticizing if you if you like  the israeli army  but i can tell you that lebanese  security source told al jazeera  a moment after the israeli army reported  a security incident  that some sort of incident  or attack or reconnaissance mission but  something happened along this border al  jazeera zaina hoda reporting live there  from the lebanon side of the border with  israel let's bring in al jazeera's harry  forsett who's in west jerusalem  uh harry what's israel saying about what  happened on the border  well yes the israeli military as uh just  reporting  is saying that there was an attempt to  infiltrate by  a cell of three to five hezbollah  fighters  uh into israeli-controlled territory in  the occupied golan heights in  the shaiba farms area that they tracked  this cell before they entered israeli  territory they came into or israeli  controlled territory  they came a few meters inside that  territory and that they were driven back  the israeli military says by uh machine  gun fire tank fire  and artillery now during the course and  just after the course  of this incident the israeli military  instructed all civilians  to remain indoors in the area about an  hour later  they went back to normal procedures  allowing people  uh back onto the roads and into open  spaces once again signaling that from  the israeli perspective  things seem to have returned to a lower  level of alert and insecurity  but as far as the israelis are concerned  they're saying that there was an attempt  they have been waiting for such an  attempt for days now since that strike  inside syria in which a hezbollah  fighter was killed  and as far as they were concerned they  were preempting or responding to  such an attempt to infiltrate their  territory al jazeera  harry fawcett live in west jerusalem  harry many thanks

